# Astro
node_modules
dist
.astro

# NOTE: Hugo's build output also lands in /public (ignored above), but Astro
# conventionally keeps *source* static assets (committed to git) in a
# directory of the same name. Un-ignore Astro's public/ source assets
# specifically so they don't get swallowed by the Hugo rule above. This repo
# has no static/ dir, so Hugo has nothing that would collide with public/img
# or public/pdf (page-bundle PDFs, e.g. content/posts/cs229/*.pdf, migrated
# into public/pdf/<postslug>/ for PdfReader.astro to serve).
!/public/
/public/*
!/public/img/
!/public/pdf/
# The RÉSUMÉ button on /profile points at me.resume = "/resume.pdf". The file
# is a source asset, not build output, so it has to survive `/public/*` above —
# otherwise the button ships as a 404 on the deployed site while still working
# locally, which is exactly the failure that hides until launch.
!/public/resume.pdf

# Camera originals staged for `npm run photos`. Full-size and EXIF-bearing —
# never committed, never published. The optimized, EXIF-stripped copies the
# script writes to public/img/g/ are what ship.
/photos-inbox/


# Fonts for figures/ are fetched by figures/build.py on first run.
/figures/fonts/
